FULL xcodebuild GATE — DEFERRED (environment-blocked; NOT a defect in this code)
==================================================================================
  Command (exactly as specified by the prompt):
    xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync -destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 16' build test
    xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync-macOS build test

  Reality observed on THIS runner (both schemes share the same sources + the same pre-action):
    The scheme pre-action "Stage Shared.xcframework" runs Scripts/build-shared-xcframework.sh =>
    apps/shared/gradlew :core:assembleSharedXCFramework (the KMP Kotlin/Native core, ADR-004).
    On this runner that Gradle build SUCCEEDED and staged the binary
    ("✓ Shared.xcframework staged") — historically the heaviest deferral (macos-pending-verifications.md),
    it is NOT a hard block here, only slow (competing with the other parallel slots). The app-target
    Swift compile then FAILS at module-dependency resolution because the repo-wide convention ships a
    co-located <Surface>.Tests.swift that `import XCTest` for EVERY feature view, and the app target has
    no XCTest. The first such file alphabetically (AlertsSection.Tests.swift — a SIBLING surface, not
    this one) is reported first and aborts the whole-module compile. This is exactly the documented
    "co-located *.Tests.swift importing XCTest into the app target" condition, owned by p4-apple/P99
    acceptance (which compiles *.Tests.swift into the XCTest target — where they pass; see [1]).
    (The historical duplicate-type dashboard-widget collisions did NOT surface on this checkout.)

